casebook d-30cfr-75_1103-5-mine-co-warning-draft v1
source "D-30cfr-75.1103-5-mine-co-warning.txt" dated 2026-10-14 by "drafted by anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 from the manual; not yet approved"
note "UNAPPROVED DRAFT: written by a language model from D-30cfr-75.1103-5-mine-co-warning.txt. Every declaration below cites the sentence"
note "it came from. Check each against the manual, add what the manual does not say, then delete"
note "this note to approve. quorum studio will not build a chip image while it is here."

# manual: "When the carbon monoxide level reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level at any sensor location"
observe co_high "carbon monoxide is 10 ppm or more above the established ambient level at a sensor"

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning"
observe sensor_warning "a sensor indicates a warning"

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
observe operator_no_hazard "the mine operator determines the signal does not present a hazard to miners"

# manual: "If any fire detection component becomes inoperative"
observe component_inoperative "a fire detection component is inoperative"

# manual: "When a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location"
observe signal_received "a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location"

# manual: "after the belt is stopped"
observe belt_stopped "the belt has been stopped"

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made as prescribed in § 75.1103-4(e)"
observe examination_made "an examination for hot rollers and fire has been made"

# manual: "any change in this information"
observe map_info_changed "the sensor locations or intended air flow direction shown on the map or schematic have changed"

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
observe map_updated "the map or schematic has been updated within 24 hours of the change"

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
observe emergency_response_duty "miners are assigned emergency response duties"

# manual: "If the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors"
observe calibration_warning "the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors"

# manual: "If one sensor becomes inoperative"
observe one_sensor_inoperative "one sensor has become inoperative"

# manual: "If two or more adjacent sensors become inoperative"
observe adjacent_sensors_inoperative "two or more adjacent sensors have become inoperative"

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative"
observe complete_system_inoperative "the complete fire detection system has become inoperative"

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section"
observe monitoring_in_progress "trained persons are conducting monitoring for carbon monoxide under this section"

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
observe operator_knows_source_safe "the mine operator knows the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"

# manual: "Handheld detectors used to monitor the belt entry under this section"
observe handheld_detectors_in_use "handheld detectors are used to monitor the belt entry under this section"

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
excuse operator_cleared "operator has determined the signal is not a hazard to miners" needs operator_no_hazard

# manual: "immediate action must be taken to repair the component"
claim detection_impaired "fire detection component inoperative and needs repair" severity 4 needs component_inoperative

# manual: "When the carbon monoxide level reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level at any sensor location, automatic fire sensor and warning device systems shall provide an effective warning signal at the following locations"
claim co_warning "carbon monoxide warning level reached, so a warning signal is required" severity 5 needs co_high

# manual: "The automatic fire sensor and warning device system shall be monitored for a period of 4 hours after the belt is stopped"
claim monitoring_required "the fire sensor and warning system must be monitored for 4 hours after the belt stops" severity 4 needs belt_stopped

# manual: "When a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location, the sensors that are activated must be identified and appropriate personnel immediately notified"
claim notify_needed "activated sensors must be identified and appropriate personnel notified" severity 5 needs signal_received

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning, the following actions must be taken"
claim evacuation_needed "miners in the affected areas must be withdrawn to a safe location" severity 8 needs sensor_warning

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
claim map_update_due "the map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of a change" severity 3 needs map_info_changed

# manual: "appropriate personnel must immediately initiate an investigation to determine the cause of the malfunction or warning signal"
claim investigation_needed "on a malfunction or warning signal, an investigation into its cause must be started immediately" severity 5 needs signal_received

# manual: "Appropriate personnel must notify miners in affected working sections, in affected areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, and at other locations specified in the approved mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction"
claim miner_notice_needed "on a sensor warning, miners in affected sections and other designated locations must be notified" severity 7 needs sensor_warning

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
excuse assigned_emergency_duty "miners assigned emergency response duties are not withdrawn" needs emergency_response_duty

# manual: "personnel manning the surface location must be notified prior to and upon completion of calibration"
claim calibration_notice_needed "personnel manning the surface location must be notified before and after calibration that will activate the warning signal" severity 3 needs calibration_warning

# manual: "Affected working sections, areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, or other areas designated in the approved emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration."
claim calibration_area_notice_needed "affected working sections and other designated areas must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration that will activate the warning signal" severity 3 needs calibration_warning

# manual: "If one sensor becomes inoperative, a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
claim sensor_monitoring_needed "a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor" severity 4 needs one_sensor_inoperative

# manual: "If two or more adjacent sensors become inoperative, trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
claim area_patrol_needed "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide, traveling them in their entirety each hour" severity 4 needs adjacent_sensors_inoperative

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative, trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
claim system_patrol_needed "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas, traveling them in their entirety each hour" severity 5 needs complete_system_inoperative

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must have two-way voice communication capability, at intervals not to exceed 2,000 feet"
claim monitor_comm_needed "monitoring persons must have two-way voice communication at intervals not exceeding 2,000 feet" severity 4 needs monitoring_in_progress

# manual: "must report carbon monoxide concentrations to the surface at intervals not to exceed one hour"
claim hourly_report_needed "monitoring persons must report carbon monoxide concentrations to the surface at intervals not exceeding one hour" severity 4 needs monitoring_in_progress

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
claim co_report_needed "monitoring persons must immediately report to the surface carbon monoxide 10 ppm above ambient" severity 6 needs monitoring_in_progress co_high

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
excuse source_known_safe "the operator knows the carbon monoxide source is not a hazard, so no immediate report is required" needs operator_knows_source_safe

# manual: "Handheld detectors used to monitor the belt entry under this section must have a detection level equivalent to that of the system's carbon monoxide sensors"
claim detector_level_needed "handheld detectors must have a detection level equivalent to the system's carbon monoxide sensors" severity 3 needs handheld_detectors_in_use

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
operator_cleared undercuts evacuation_needed

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made as prescribed in § 75.1103-4(e)"
examination_made rebuts monitoring_required

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
map_updated rebuts map_update_due

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
operator_cleared undercuts miner_notice_needed

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
assigned_emergency_duty undercuts evacuation_needed

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
source_known_safe undercuts co_report_needed

# manual: "All miners in the affected areas, unless assigned emergency response duties, must be immediately withdrawn to a safe location identified in the mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction."
action withdraw_miners safe when any evacuation_needed

# manual: "automatic fire sensor and warning device systems shall provide an effective warning signal at the following locations"
action raise_alarm when any co_warning

# manual: "immediate action must be taken to repair the component"
action repair_component when any detection_impaired

# manual: "While repairs are being made, operation of the belt may continue if the following requirements are met"
action keep_running idle

# manual: "the sensors that are activated must be identified and appropriate personnel immediately notified"
action notify_personnel when any notify_needed

# manual: "The automatic fire sensor and warning device system shall be monitored for a period of 4 hours after the belt is stopped"
action monitor_system when any monitoring_required

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
action update_map when any map_update_due

# manual: "appropriate personnel must immediately initiate an investigation to determine the cause of the malfunction or warning signal"
action investigate_cause when any investigation_needed

# manual: "Appropriate personnel must notify miners in affected working sections, in affected areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, and at other locations specified in the approved mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction"
action notify_miners when any miner_notice_needed

# manual: "personnel manning the surface location must be notified prior to and upon completion of calibration"
action notify_surface_personnel when any calibration_notice_needed

# manual: "Affected working sections, areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, or other areas designated in the approved emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration."
action notify_calibration_areas when any calibration_area_notice_needed

# manual: "a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
action monitor_inoperative_sensor when any sensor_monitoring_needed

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
action patrol_affected_areas when any area_patrol_needed

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
action patrol_whole_system when any system_patrol_needed

# manual: "Alternatively, a trained person must be stationed at each inoperative sensor to monitor for carbon monoxide"
action station_person_at_sensors when any area_patrol_needed

# manual: "must have two-way voice communication capability, at intervals not to exceed 2,000 feet"
action provide_voice_communication when any monitor_comm_needed

# manual: "must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
action report_co_to_surface when any co_report_needed hourly_report_needed

# manual: "must have a detection level equivalent to that of the system's carbon monoxide sensors"
action use_equivalent_detectors when any detector_level_needed

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
prefer withdraw_miners over raise_alarm over report_co_to_surface over notify_miners over notify_personnel over notify_surface_personnel over notify_calibration_areas over investigate_cause over monitor_inoperative_sensor over patrol_affected_areas over station_person_at_sensors over patrol_whole_system over provide_voice_communication over use_equivalent_detectors over monitor_system over repair_component over update_map over keep_running
